  "79335513": [
   {
    "answer_id": 79486079,
    "body": "<p>Just re open your debeaver as an administrator.That worked for me</p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1741168851,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 10
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79785794,
    "body": "<p>I was facing the same issue with an Azure VM using Windows. Here was the fix:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Uncheck &quot;Use Windows trust store&quot;:</strong></p>\n<p>On DBeaver, when using Windows, navigating to <code>Window &gt; Preferences &gt; Connections</code> and unchecking &quot;Use Windows trust store&quot;.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/a/48593318\">https://stackoverflow.com/a/48593318</a></p>\n<p>I hope that helps.</p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1759951017,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 5
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79383023,
    "body": "<p>This happened because DBeaver can't download driver via the Internet for some reason.</p>\n<p>However you can install Postgres driver manually by:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Downloading Postgres driver file <code>postgresql-42.X.X.jar</code> using the link: <a href=\"https://jdbc.postgresql.org/download/\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jdbc.postgresql.org/download/</a></p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Put <code>.JAR</code> file into this path (if there's no directory, create one)</p>\n<p><code>%APPDATA%\\DBeaverData\\drivers\\maven\\unknown\\org.postgresql</code></p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Try to establish the Connection again.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n",
    "creation_date": 1737681880,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 3
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79655699,
    "body": "<p>just put new driver inside AppData\\Local\\DBeaver\\plugins</p>\n<p>drivers here <a href=\"https://jdbc.postgresql.org/download/\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jdbc.postgresql.org/download/</a></p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1749201612,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 0
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79562664,
    "body": "<p>I open with sudo and work for me.</p>\n<p>On terminal, write:</p>\n<pre><code>sudo dbeaver\n</code></pre>\n<p>If you work on Linux,  will work fine.</p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1744131670,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": -1
   }
  ],
  "79339258": [
   {
    "answer_id": 79339565,
    "body": "<p>I was having the same problem. I even tried to change the node and npm mirror, but same error. I just rolled back to <a href=\"https://github.com/coreybutler/nvm-windows/releases/tag/1.1.12\" rel=\"noreferrer\">nvm version 1.1.12</a> and it worked just fine.</p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1736346835,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 85
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79346319,
    "body": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/coreybutler/nvm-windows/issues/1209\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://github.com/coreybutler/nvm-windows/issues/1209</a></p>\n<p>Bug in NVM-Windows - planned to be fixed in next version</p>\n<p>Potentially useful workaround is to go back to a previous NVM version like v1.1.12</p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1736525792,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 49
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79646900,
    "body": "<p>Solution for those who use NVM via Chocolatey:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open CMD or PowerShell as Administrator.</li>\n<li>Copy and execute this command:\n<pre class=\"lang-bash prettyprint-override\"><code>choco install --force --version 1.1.12 nvm.install\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n<li>Enter <code>A</code> when asked.</li>\n<li>If you get a dialogue box by NVM asking to take control of your already installed different versions of Node then just click on <code>Yes</code> button.</li>\n<li>Keep clicking on <code>Yes</code> button if the dialogue box keeps appearing again and again.</li>\n</ul>\n",
    "creation_date": 1748717462,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 7
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79990153,
    "body": "<p>Just had this issue and this is how I solved it.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Go to Node's oficial download page <a href=\"https://nodejs.org/en/download\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://nodejs.org/en/download</a> and download the version you want as a <em><strong>.zip (Standalone Binary)</strong></em></p>\n</li>\n<li><p>After you download the version you want extract it in your computer, the folder should have a name like <em><strong>node-v24.19.0-win-x64,</strong></em> change the name of the folder and only leave the version number for example <em><strong>v24.19.0</strong></em>.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Go to your terminal and type <em><strong>nvm root</strong></em>, this will list where the base folder of your nvm instance is stored. <em>If you have other versions of node installed you should see some other folders with names like yours.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Copy the folder you renamed to the nvm root folder in my case C:\\Users\\<em><strong>User</strong></em>\\AppData\\Local\\nvm.<br />\nRun nvm list and the new version should show up!</p>\n<p>Btw, I'm currently using <em><strong>nvm version 1.2.2</strong></em></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n",
    "creation_date": 1785772707,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 2
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79527714,
    "body": "<p>I had a similar error when installing the old version of nodejs 0.12.2.\nI need this version to work with the old version of WebOS 3.4 installed on my TV.</p>\n<p>Before that, I already had nodejs versions 23.10.0 and 16.20.2 installed</p>\n<p>I downloaded the node-v0.12.2 Win-x64.msi installer from here <a href=\"https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v0.12.2\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v0.12.2</a> and installed it in the default folder (let's say it was the C:\\nvm4w\\nodejs_0.12.2 folder. It doesn't matter now).</p>\n<p>After installation, the following files were in the folder:\n<a href=\"https://i.sstatic.net/md9ihMXD.jpg\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">Installed Nodejs 0.12.2 files</a>\nI checked, the nodejs version 0.12.2 was not listed anywhere. I searched and found that versions 23.10.0 and 16.20.2 are present in the folders of the same name C:\\Users\\KS\\AppData\\Local\\nvm. By analogy, I created a folder v0.12.2 and dropped the contents obtained during the installation of node-v0.12.2 Win-x64.msi into it.</p>\n<p>The result was as follows:\n<a href=\"https://i.sstatic.net/FyS0JhsV.jpg\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">Folder with all installed versions of Nodejs</a>\nWhen unsuccessfully attempting to install Nodejs 0.12.2 with the command nvm install 0.12.2\nthe file npm-v2.7.4.zip was downloaded to the folder C:\\Users\\KS\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\nvm-install-3885601035\\temp\nBut for some reason the installer was looking for this file in the folder C:\\Users\\KS\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\nvm-npm-2168612958. There was such a folder, but it was empty\n<a href=\"https://i.sstatic.net/Oln0XIo1.jpg\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">Error &quot;Cannot find the npm file&quot;</a>\nI took the file npm-v2.7.4.zip, unpacked it into a separate folder and ran the command nvm use 0.12.2 (this is mandatory!)\nIn the folder C:\\nvm4w\\nodejs (the appearance of which changes depending on the version of nodejs used) I created the node_modules folder, in it I created the npm folder, and in it (that is, in the folder C:\\nvm4w\\nodejs\\node_modules\\npm) I put all the contents of the npm-v2.7.4.zip archive.</p>\n<p>Now, when using Nodejs version 0.12.2, everything is the same as when using Nodejs version 16.20.2 and 23.10.0\n<a href=\"https://i.sstatic.net/EkkxvWZP.jpg\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">Installed Nodejs versions</a>\nAccordingly, the command is executed\n<a href=\"https://i.sstatic.net/WxYqb6wX.jpg\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">For Nodejs 0.12.2 npm 2.74 is used</a></p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1742659682,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 1
   }
  ],
  "79358893": [
   {
    "answer_id": 79358969,
    "body": "<p>It's an intermittent issue and is reported on: <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/390105581\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Uncaught TypeError: vb.X is not a constructor</a>. You may <code>+1</code> on it to let Google know you're also experiencing the same problem.</p>\n<p>As of now, the latest update on Google's end is comment <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/390105581#comment107\" rel=\"noreferrer\">#107</a> from <code>jp...@google.com&lt;jp...@google.com&gt;</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I am locking comments for this issue as no additional information is needed by the engineering team. Currently, a fix is being rolled out to production. You can <a href=\"https://developers.google.com/issue-tracker/guides/subscribe\" rel=\"noreferrer\">subscribe</a> to this issue by clicking the star \u2b50 button. Thank you for your patience.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>UPDATE</h3>\n<p>As of <code>Jan 16, 2025 05:10AM</code> PhST, comment <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/390105581#comment108\" rel=\"noreferrer\">#108</a> from <code>jp...@google.com&lt;jp...@google.com&gt;</code> verifies that:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Marked as fixed.\nThis issue has been fixed.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr />\n<h3>SUMMARY</h3>\n<p>Numerous users reported getting the error <code>Uncaught TypeError: vb.X is not a constructor</code> on their Google Apps Script web apps. The issue is intermittent and is sometimes resolved by doing a refresh on the page. Google implemented a fix with no further action required by its users, and the issue is now resolved.</p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1736957798,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 16
   }
  ],
  "79363302": [
   {
    "answer_id": 79421904,
    "body": "<p>It's a new feature for <a href=\"https://code.visualstudio.com/updates/v1_97#_svg-image-preview-support\" rel=\"noreferrer\">last version</a>.</p>\n<p>Go to settings, search for <code>workbench.editorAssociations</code> and add item with key <code>*.svg</code> and value <code>default</code></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://i.sstatic.net/I1Vt6DWk.png\" alt=\"screenshot of setting\" /></p>\n<p>I found this solution <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/vscode/comments/1ibntfy/svg_files_open_as_previews_i_want_them_to_open_as/\" rel=\"noreferrer\" title=\"SVG files open as previews, I want them to open as text files\">on Reddit</a>.</p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1738954661,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 120
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79427278,
    "body": "<p>VS Code was recently updated to render SVG files as previews by default.</p>\n<p>Paste this in your <code>settings.json</code> to disable the feature:</p>\n<pre><code>&quot;workbench.editorAssociations&quot;: {\n    &quot;*.svg&quot;: &quot;default&quot;\n}\n</code></pre>\n",
    "creation_date": 1739195344,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 42
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79363385,
    "body": "<p>You can do one of two things.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Right-click on the file in the Explorer, or right-click on the tab after opening the file, and choose <code>Open With...</code> and then select the <code>Text Editor</code> option and you should get the svg code.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>You can set the default to be to open svg files in a text editor instead of an image preview from that same context menu.  Choose the <code>Configure default editor for *.svg files</code> and it will always open in a text editor thereafter.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n",
    "creation_date": 1737074484,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 23
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79600702,
    "body": "<p>The accepted answer did not work for me. This did, credit <a href=\"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/239844#issuecomment-2705545349\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/239844#issuecomment-2705545349</a></p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Right click on the svg file in the sidebar</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Open With...</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Configure default editor for &quot;*.svg&quot;</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Text Editor (built in)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Now I can actually read svg file code again.</p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1746028804,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 1
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79842222,
    "body": "<p>Go to <code>File -&gt; Preferences -&gt; Settings</code>, then in search field type &quot;preview&quot;, at the bottom (i.e. somewhere else) there is option &quot;SVG preview &quot;, click to open, and uncheck &quot;Automatically open the preview when an svg file is opened.&quot;</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://i.sstatic.net/zOd4j9W5.png\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://i.sstatic.net/zOd4j9W5.png\" alt=\"enter image description here\" /></a></p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1765301903,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 0
   }
