    "body": "<p>Just use <strong>gemini-flash-latest</strong></p>\n<p>All models: <a href=\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models</a></p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1759317331,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 42
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79790844,
    "body": "<ol>\n<li><p><strong>It is not only the model version, it is also related to how you import the SDK:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Old SDK:</strong> <code>@google/generative-ai</code> \u2192 deprecated</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>New SDK:</strong> <code>@google/genai</code> \u2192 supported and actively maintained</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<pre><code>import { GoogleGenAI } from '@google/genai';\nconst ai = new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY });\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>Update the model name:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Old:</strong> <code>gemini-1.5-flash-latest</code> \u2192 deprecated</li>\n<li><strong>New:</strong> <code>gemini-2.0-flash</code> or <code>gemini-2.5-flash</code> \u2192 available</li>\n</ul>\n<pre><code>const modelName = 'gemini-2.5-flash';\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n</ol>\n",
    "creation_date": 1760508633,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 7
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79831124,
    "body": "<p>I had this same issue in my node server. The code was working fine last month, but unexpectedly it started throwing this error. Then I found out that Google has moved some of its AI models recently.</p>\n<p>Just hit the below API using e.g., Postman and that will eventually give you the list of AI model names that you can you with your API key.</p>\n<pre><code>https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models?key=&gt;&lt;Your Gemini API Key&gt; \n</code></pre>\n<p>(Hit this if the error says it could not find the given model in the API version v1Beta)</p>\n<pre><code>https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models?key=&lt;Your Gemini API Key&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<p>(Hit this if the error says it could not find the given model in the API version v1)</p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1764187705,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 5
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79807685,
    "body": "<p>I had this error too, but replaced &quot;gemini-1.5-flash&quot; with the following code. It works fine now.</p>\n<pre><code>\n    modelName = &quot;gemini-2.5-pro&quot;\n</code></pre>\n",
