    "answer_id": 79847232,
    "body": "<p>These folders are projected from the Nuget package (EntityFrameworkCore.Design).</p>\n<p>Seems like they are now needed for dotnet-ef operations (e.g. migrations). The folders are also copied to the publishing output, what I would consider a bug (they are not needed at runtime).</p>\n<p>At least you could hide them from the solution/project view by adding this section to your .csproj file(s):</p>\n<pre class=\"lang-xml prettyprint-override\"><code>&lt;ItemGroup&gt;\n    &lt;Content Update=&quot;@(Content)&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;Visible Condition=&quot;'%(NuGetItemType)' == 'Content'&quot;&gt;false&lt;/Visible&gt;\n    &lt;/Content&gt;\n&lt;/ItemGroup&gt;\n</code></pre>\n",
    "creation_date": 1765744280,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 23
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79887781,
    "body": "<p>Upgrading &quot;Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design&quot; to version 10.0.2 or greater solves the issue. No need for workarounds.</p>\n",
    "creation_date": 1770852486,
    "is_accepted": false,
    "score": 10
   },
   {
    "answer_id": 79865301,
    "body": "<pre><code>&lt;PackageReference Include=&quot;Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design&quot; Version=&quot;10.0.1&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;IncludeAssets&gt;runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive&lt;/IncludeAssets&gt;\n  &lt;PrivateAssets&gt;all&lt;/PrivateAssets&gt;\n&lt;/PackageReference&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<p>Removing <code>contentfiles</code> from <code>IncludeAssets</code> worked for me!</p>\n",
